    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "Perfect! All tests are passing. Here's a summary of the fixes I made:\n\n## Summary\n\nI fixed the two failing tests in the frai-core test suite:\n\n### 1. **Fixed toxicityMetric in `src/eval/metrics.js`**\n   - **Problem**: The function was accepting `bannedTerms` as a second parameter, which was being populated with the `references` array when called by `runEvaluations()`. This caused the references to be misinterpreted as banned terms, incorrectly flagging safe content as toxic.\n   - **Solution**: Changed `toxicityMetric` to only accept the `outputs` parameter and always use the default banned terms, ignoring any second argument passed by `runEvaluations()`.\n\n### 2. **Added named exports in `src/finetune/index.js`**\n   - **Problem**: The test file was trying to import `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export, but the module only exported it in the default export object.\n   - **Solution**: Added named exports for the schema constants (`APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, `RISK_LEVELS`) so they can be imported directly.\n\n**Results**: \n- \u2705 All 28 tests passing across 8 test files\n- \u2705 All public exports remain intact and functional\n- \u2705 No test files were modified; only source code was fixed",
